ce=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bruchfl%C3%A4che_eines_Perlmuttst%C3%BCcks.JPG/500px-Bruchfl%C3%A4che_eines_Perlmuttst%C3%BCcks.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Electron microscopy image of a fractured surface of nacre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABruchfl%C3%A4che_eines_Perlmuttst%C3%BCcks.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf/page1-500px-PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf/page1-1280px-PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf/page1-500px-PearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Formation of non–bead-cultured Akoya \"keshi\" pearls produced in a P. i. fucata mollusk. (A) Optical overview of a nonbeaded keshi–cultured pearl. (B) Cross-section showing CaCO3 growth begins onto an organic center. (C) Mature nacre. (D and E) Atomic-resolution image of atoms in nacre. (F) Transition from spherulitic aragonite structures to nacre. (G and H) Aggregated nanoparticles form massive aragonite. (I) The formation of nacre begins directly on massive aragonite.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APearlCrossSection_Figure1.pdf"}],"sounds":{"pearl":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/72/En-au-pearl.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/72/En-au-pearl.ogg/En-au-pearl.ogg.mp3"}]}}}